   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +1 / -0",
   "html": "<p>\n\tWhich of the following statement(s) is/are correct?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>\n\tPre-emphasis is the process of artificial boosting of high frequency components of <em>m</em>(<em>t</em>) to increase corresponding SNR.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Generally, a low pass filter is used to perform de-emphasis."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "For audio signal pre-emphasis and de-emphasis is not required whereas for video signal preemphasis and de-emphasis is required."
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "First stage of the receiver contributes the maximum to the noise figure of the receiver."
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
