  {
   "n": 28,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is not correct?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "In modulation, base band signal is converted to bandpass signal."
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Amplitude modulation are non-linear modulation scheme whereas angle modulation are linear modulation scheme."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "Phase modulation is non-linear modulation scheme."
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "Limiter is used to eliminate the noise effects in a FM detector."
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "B"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.66
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\t&bull; The purpose of the limiter is to provide a constant level of the signal to the FM demodulator, thus reducing the effect of signal level changes in the output.<br />\n\t&bull; Amplitude modulation are linear modulation scheme whereas angle modulation are non-linear modulation scheme.<br />\n\t&bull; In modulation, base band signal is converted to bandpass signal, whereby the signal is shifted to a higher frequency range.</p>"
  },
